[agent:result]         """List model versions. You can list model versions under a particular schema, or list all model versions
[agent:result]         in the current metastore.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]         The returned models are filtered based on the privileges of the calling user. For example, the
[agent:result]         metastore admin is able to list all the model versions. A regular user needs to be the owner or have
[agent:result]         the **EXECUTE** privilege on the parent registered model to recieve the model versions in the
[agent:result]         response. For the latter case, the caller must also be the owner or have the **USE_CATALOG** privilege
[agent:result]         on the parent catalog and the **USE_SCHEMA** privilege on the parent schema.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]         There is no guarantee of a specific ordering of the elements in the response. The elements in the
[agent:result]         response will not contain any aliases or tags.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]         PAGINATION BEHAVIOR: The API is by default paginated, a page may contain zero results while still
[agent:result]         providing a next_page_token. Clients must continue reading pages until next_page_token is absent,
[agent:result]         which is the only indication that the end of results has been reached.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]         :param full_name: str
[agent:result]           The full three-level name of the registered model under which to list model versions
[agent:result]         :param include_browse: bool (optional)
[agent:result]           Whether to include model versions in the response for which the principal can only access selective
[agent:result]           metadata for
[agent:result]         :param max_results: int (optional)
[agent:result]           Maximum number of model versions to return. If not set, the page length is set to a server
[agent:result]           configured value (100, as of 1/3/2024). - when set to a value greater than 0, the page length is the
[agent:result]           minimum of this value and a server configured value(1000, as of 1/3/2024); - when set to 0, the page
[agent:result]           length is set to a server configured value (100, as of 1/3/2024) (recommended); - when set to a
[agent:result]           value less than 0, an invalid parameter error is returned;
[agent:result]         :param page_token: str (optional)
[agent:result]           Opaque pagination token to go to next page based on previous query.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]         :returns: Iterator over :class:`ModelVersionInfo`
[agent:result]         """
[agent:result] 
